# Byte identity is the whole point of this package. to_run.py refuses to start if any frozen file's
# SHA-256 differs from manifests/vendored_sha256.json, and git's end-of-line translation is a silent
# byte change: with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) every .py and .md here would arrive with
# CRLF, every hash would differ, and gate A-V1 would abort a perfectly honest clone.
#
# So: no translation, in either direction, for anything in this directory. What was committed is what
# is checked out, on every platform.
* -text
